course: dictionary
lesson: 5992
title: What does meaning mean?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word meaning has several jobs. A word's meaning is what the word stands for. «Losing or changing one small word can change a whole meaning.» So a meaning is the message the words carry, and one small change can change that message.
explain: Meaning can also mean purpose or importance, and a hidden message. «Pysanky are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye, with patterns that carry meanings like the sun, wheat or waves.» Here the meanings are the ideas the patterns stand for, such as the sun for light or wheat for a good harvest.
explain: Be a detective: when you see meaning, ask which job it is doing. In maths, + means add. In «I've been meaning to call you», it is a form of mean that means planning to.
fact: The meaning of a word or sign is what it stands for or expresses.
fact: The meaning of something can be its purpose or importance, as in «the meaning of life».
fact: The hidden message or idea behind something is also its meaning, as in «the meaning of a poem».
fact: «Meaning» is the -ing form of mean: «I've been meaning to call you» means you have planned to call.
fact: Most words are arbitrary: the link between a word and its meaning is a habit of the speakers, not something in nature.
exercise: In maths, the sign + means what? | Take away | Divide | *Add | Equals
exercise: «I've been meaning to call you.» What does this show? | You cannot call at all | You have already called | *You have planned to call for a while | You are cross with them
exercise: «Pysanky… carry meanings like the sun, wheat or waves.» What does meanings mean here? | The prices of the eggs | The days of the week | Eggs that float in water | *The ideas the patterns stand for
test: «Losing or changing one small word can change a whole meaning.» What does meaning mean in this sentence? | *The message or idea the words give | The length of the sentence | The name of the writer | The number of letters
test: What is the meaning of a word? | A word that rhymes with it | *What the word stands for | Shouting it loudly | Its spelling only
exam: In «a life full of meaning», what does meaning mean? | *Purpose and importance | The colour of life | Sadness and tears | The number of years we live
